# judge-compute-suggestion

EXPORT TEMPLATE judge-compute-suggestion:
  ABOUT   judge rule for every DO line the agent carries out itself — a calculation is better left to a COMPUTE block
  APPLIES #judge #agent
  SLOTS:
    action: TEXT  "a line the agent carries out"
      SHOULD-NOT  describe a calculation that a deterministic program could carry out exactly, with no judgment, interpretation or writing
        YES  counting, summing, converting, sorting, filtering, date arithmetic, formatting or checking a value against a stated rule, on values the line already has — the same input always gives the same right output
        NO   it needs judgment, interpretation, understanding or writing of language, choosing, explaining, or talking to someone — or it reads, extracts or copies values out of a file, a document or a text
  BODY:
    DO {action}
  EXAMPLE:
    sum the totals of invoices → a calculation: a program could do it
    write a polite reminder to the client → needs judgment and language
    keep only the rows of table where status is open → a calculation: a program could do it
    decide which bug to fix first → needs judgment
    read the amounts printed on the receipt file → needs reading a document
    read the deadline from the request file the user names → needs reading a document
